Investigation 6 - Checkout Transaction Duration and Lock-Holding Time
Run: 20261127T121501Z_7384c1d4; one instrumented trial; all timing values below are milliseconds unless labelled seconds.

Outcome: 400 buyers; 50 successful purchases; 350 out-of-stock refusals; 0 errors; final stock 0.
Workload wall time: 21.109016 seconds.
Before barrier release (thread startup, connection establishment, barrier): 11.330176 seconds.
After barrier release through connection closure and joins: 9.778840 seconds.
Wall time excludes fixture/schema installation, clock calibration and post-run validation/cleanup.
This is a diagnostic-copy run, not an execution of the official race_test.py.

Confirmed transaction boundary:
- race_test.py opens one connection per worker, enables autocommit, waits at the 400-worker barrier, executes the checkout SELECT, fetches the result and closes the connection.
- No explicit commit() call occurs in official workers. Each SELECT runs in its own implicit transaction. The function return does not itself release the product-row lock; it remains held until transaction end.
- The diagnostic runner uses the same worker connection/barrier/autocommit boundary, without extra per-worker clock queries or explicit commits.
- All 400 worker connections reported transaction status IDLE after checkout execute/fetch, confirming no open transaction remained at that point.
- Official fire() wall time includes opening connections, barrier wait, checkout, closing connections and thread joins; per-call elapsed excludes connection establishment.

Timing table: average / median / maximum (ms). Dash means operation did not execute.
